    summary: "SVG and CorelDRAW (CDR) represent the two premier vector standards for responsive web engineering and physical prepress manufacturing, respectively. While SVG delivers lightweight, DOM-accessible, scriptable graphics for modern browsers, CDR excels at multipage desktop publishing, high-precision CAD drafting, spot color separations, and automated cutting plotter workflows. By understanding the structural differences between open XML text and proprietary packaged containers, managing color shifts between sRGB and CMYK, converting live typography to permanent B\\u00e9zier curves, and adhering to strict dimensional coordinate standards, designers can bridge digital web assets and commercial print manufacturing without loss of fidelity. Use Navorika's client-side vector conversion suite to translate assets safely and instantly between SVG and CDR.",
